    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite runs green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` case.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new, `rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a public helper following the established `CheckDigit.of(...)` / `MembershipLevel.of(...)` pattern. `of(\"+61412345678\")` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`: it splits off the country code, then groups the national digits in threes. Non-canonical values are returned unchanged, and `null` maps to `null`.\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a package-private `splitCountryCode(digits)` that reuses the existing `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` table (longest-code-first, so `+61` wins over `+1`), so display splitting stays consistent with normalization. Unknown codes fall back to a 2-digit assumption so display never crashes.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"telephoneDisplay\", expression = \"...TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())\")` alongside the other derived-field mappings.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nThe change is purely additive to the response DTO \u2014 the raw `telephone` field is untouched.",
